" vimtris.normal.keys - vimtris played by Vim's normal mode: keystrokes, no Vim script.
"
" This file is a buffer, and the game is the editing of it. Lines 1 and 2 and
" the 23 lines of board below them have fixed places; everything else is
" found by searching for it. The launcher (vimtris.sh) loads the file into
" vim -es and, for every input line (the seed, then one event per line),
" types four commands:
"
"   :norm! ggS<input>                 the input goes into line 1
"   :norm! 2G"ay$@a                   yank line 2 into register a and run it
"   :/^F$/+1,/^E$/-1w >>/dev/stdout   the frame, between the lines F and E
"   :norm! @q                         register q is ZQ once the game is over
"
" Everything else is normal mode: motions, searches, yanks, edits, and @ to
" run a register. The keys are written <Esc>, <CR>, <C-A>, <C-X>, <C-R> and
" <C-V>; the launcher turns them into the bytes before Vim reads the file.
"
" Control flow:
"
" - A failing command (a search that finds nothing, a motion off the line)
"   aborts every key still waiting, all the way out to the :norm. So no
"   command here may fail, and a failure can't be used as an if.
" - Code lives on lines ":name keys". A call is /^:name <CR>f l"ay$@a: find
"   the line, yank the keys after the name, run them. When they are done,
"   the keys after the call run on: @ puts a register in front of the keys
"   still waiting, so this is a real call that returns.
" - An if is a search that can't fail: gg/<pattern>\|^ELSE|<CR>. Every line
"   it can land on ends in |@s (the pattern matched) or |@f (it landed on
"   the ELSE line), and $h"ay$@a runs that ending. @s and @f are trampolines:
"   they call the code named on the "then" and "else" lines, which the code
"   sets just before the search.
" - A search finds the first match in the buffer, so every fallback (ELSE,
"   :evx, PAINTED) comes after what it stands in for.
" - Loops are calls of themselves from a branch, at the end of the code, so
"   the waiting keys don't pile up.
"
" Numbers are decimal text, changed with <C-A> and <C-X> and a count. Vim
" caps a count at 999999999, so 2^31 - 1 is three counts, and the seed is
" multiplied by 7 digit by digit, from a table. A count can't start with 0
" either (0 is a motion), which is why the row is kept as y + 3 (its line
" number) and the column as x + 5. A command that needs a number from the
" buffer as its count is typed into the "cmd" line with <C-R> and yanked
" into register b to run.
"
" The board is lines 3 to 22: four walls, ten cells, four walls, and |@s.
" Three lines of floor follow. A piece fits if a search like
" \%3l\%8c\.\_.\{20}\.\.\. finds its four empty cells at its line and column:
" \_. crosses the ends of lines, and a board line is 22 bytes with its
" newline. The F lines hold that regex for each piece and rotation, the S
" lines the motions and r<letter> that write the piece into the board.
"
" ---- the state: "name value", found with /^name <CR>w
mode new|@s
seed 0|@s
row 3|@s
col 8|@s
rot 0|@s
cur I
nxt I
drawn I
tick 0|@s
level 1|@s
lines 0|@s
tolevel 10|@s
score 0|@s
w 0|@s
chk 0|@s
k 0
dig |@s
rem 0
mul |@s
prod |@s
carry 0|@s
cmd x
then nop
else nop
:s /^then <CR>w"nyiw/^:<C-R>n <CR>f l"ay$@a
:f /^else <CR>w"nyiw/^:<C-R>n <CR>f l"ay$@a
" ---- the code: ":name keys". :s and :f are the trampolines of an if.
" Every input: the seed while "mode" is new, else an event.
:main /^then <CR>wcwboot<Esc>/^else <CR>wcwevent<Esc>gg/^mode new\|^ELSE|<CR>ml$h"ay$@a
" The seed: draw the next piece, then spawn (which draws the one after).
:boot /^mode <CR>wcwplay<Esc>gg"ny$/^seed <CR>wcw<C-R>n<Esc>/^:q0 <CR>f l"qy$/^:draw <CR>f l"ay$@a/^drawn <CR>w"nyl/^nxt <CR>ws<C-R>n<Esc>/^:spawn <CR>f l"ay$@a
" Run :ev<input>, or :evx (nothing) for an unknown code.
:event gg"ny$/\V\^:ev<C-R>n \|\^:evx <CR>f l"ay$@a
:nop gg
" Tick: chk = tick + level - 11; at 0 or more the piece falls (every max(1, 11 - level) ticks).
:ev0 /^tick <CR>w<C-A>/^tick <CR>w"nyiw/^chk <CR>wC<C-R>n|@s<Esc>/^level <CR>w"nyiw/^cmd <CR>wC<C-R>n<C-V><C-A><Esc>04l"by$/^chk <CR>w@b11<C-X>/^then <CR>wcwfall<Esc>/^else <CR>wcwnop<Esc>gg/^chk \d\|^ELSE|<CR>ml$h"ay$@a
:fall /^tick <CR>wcw0<Esc>/^:ev4 <CR>f l"ay$@a
" Left: one column left; if it does not fit, back.
:ev1 /^col <CR>w<C-X>/^then <CR>wcwframe<Esc>/^else <CR>wcwundol<Esc>/^:fit <CR>f l"ay$@a
:undol /^col <CR>w<C-A>/^:frame <CR>f l"ay$@a
:ev2 /^col <CR>w<C-A>/^then <CR>wcwframe<Esc>/^else <CR>wcwundor<Esc>/^:fit <CR>f l"ay$@a
:undor /^col <CR>w<C-X>/^:frame <CR>f l"ay$@a
" Rotate: the next rotation at the kicks 0, -1, +1, -2, +2 (k1 ... k5), or back.
:ev3 /^rot <CR>w<C-A>/^then <CR>wcwrot0<Esc>/^else <CR>wcwnop<Esc>gg/^rot 4\|^ELSE|<CR>ml$h"ay$@a/^then <CR>wcwframe<Esc>/^else <CR>wcwk1<Esc>/^:fit <CR>f l"ay$@a
:rot0 /^rot <CR>wr0
:k1 /^col <CR>w<C-X>/^then <CR>wcwframe<Esc>/^else <CR>wcwk2<Esc>/^:fit <CR>f l"ay$@a
:k2 /^col <CR>w2<C-A>/^then <CR>wcwframe<Esc>/^else <CR>wcwk3<Esc>/^:fit <CR>f l"ay$@a
:k3 /^col <CR>w3<C-X>/^then <CR>wcwframe<Esc>/^else <CR>wcwk4<Esc>/^:fit <CR>f l"ay$@a
:k4 /^col <CR>w4<C-A>/^then <CR>wcwframe<Esc>/^else <CR>wcwk5<Esc>/^:fit <CR>f l"ay$@a
:k5 /^col <CR>w2<C-X>/^rot <CR>w<C-X>/^then <CR>wcwrot3<Esc>/^else <CR>wcwnop<Esc>gg/^rot -\|^ELSE|<CR>ml$h"ay$@a/^:frame <CR>f l"ay$@a
:rot3 /^rot <CR>w2s3<Esc>
" Soft drop, and a fall: one row down, or back up and lock.
:ev4 /^row <CR>w<C-A>/^then <CR>wcwframe<Esc>/^else <CR>wcwundod<Esc>/^:fit <CR>f l"ay$@a
:undod /^row <CR>w<C-X>/^:lock <CR>f l"ay$@a
" Hard drop: down until it does not fit, then back up and lock.
:ev5 /^row <CR>w<C-A>/^then <CR>wcwev5<Esc>/^else <CR>wcwundod<Esc>/^:fit <CR>f l"ay$@a
" The fit regex at the line and column of the piece, as an if.
:fit /^cur <CR>w"pyl/^rot <CR>w"oyl/^row <CR>w"ryiw/^col <CR>w"cyiw/^F<C-R>p<C-R>o:<CR>f:l"xy$/^cmd <CR>wC\%<C-R>rl\%<C-R>cc<C-R>x<Esc>04l"by$gg/<C-R>b\|^ELSE|<CR>ml$h"ay$@a
" Write the piece into the board, then clear the full rows (k counts them).
:lock /^:stampb <CR>f l"ay$@a/^k <CR>wcw0<Esc>/^:clear <CR>f l"ay$@a
:stampb /^row <CR>w"ryiw/^col <CR>w"cyiw/^cmd <CR>wC<C-R>rG<C-R>c|<Esc>04l"by$/^cur <CR>w"pyl/^rot <CR>w"oyl/^S<C-R>p<C-R>o:<CR>f:l"xy$@b@x
" A full row is four walls, ten letters, four walls: delete it, add an empty one on top.
:clear /^then <CR>wcwrmrow<Esc>/^else <CR>wcwscore<Esc>gg/^####[A-Z]\{10}####|\|^ELSE|<CR>ml$h"ay$@a
:rmrow 'l"_dd/^EMPTYROW<CR>j"eyy3G"eP/^k <CR>w<C-A>/^:clear <CR>f l"ay$@a
" Points for k rows (times the level), the lines, and a level every ten lines.
:score /^k <CR>w"nyl/^:pts<C-R>n <CR>f l"ay$@a/^:spawn <CR>f l"ay$@a
:pts0 gg
:pts1 /^:c40 <CR>f l"xy$/^level <CR>w"nyiw/^cmd <CR>wC<C-R>n@x<Esc>04l"by$/^score <CR>w@b/^lines <CR>w1<C-A>/^tolevel <CR>w1<C-X>/^:lvl <CR>f l"ay$@a
:c40 40<C-A>
:pts2 /^:c100 <CR>f l"xy$/^level <CR>w"nyiw/^cmd <CR>wC<C-R>n@x<Esc>04l"by$/^score <CR>w@b/^lines <CR>w2<C-A>/^tolevel <CR>w2<C-X>/^:lvl <CR>f l"ay$@a
:c100 100<C-A>
:pts3 /^:c300 <CR>f l"xy$/^level <CR>w"nyiw/^cmd <CR>wC<C-R>n@x<Esc>04l"by$/^score <CR>w@b/^lines <CR>w3<C-A>/^tolevel <CR>w3<C-X>/^:lvl <CR>f l"ay$@a
:c300 300<C-A>
:pts4 /^:c1200 <CR>f l"xy$/^level <CR>w"nyiw/^cmd <CR>wC<C-R>n@x<Esc>04l"by$/^score <CR>w@b/^lines <CR>w4<C-A>/^tolevel <CR>w4<C-X>/^:lvl <CR>f l"ay$@a
:c1200 1200<C-A>
:lvl /^then <CR>wcwlvlup<Esc>/^else <CR>wcwnop<Esc>gg/^tolevel \(-\|0|\)\|^ELSE|<CR>ml$h"ay$@a
:lvlup /^level <CR>w<C-A>/^tolevel <CR>w10<C-A>
" The next piece falls from row 0, column 3; the game is over if it does not fit.
:spawn /^nxt <CR>w"nyl/^cur <CR>ws<C-R>n<Esc>/^:draw <CR>f l"ay$@a/^drawn <CR>w"nyl/^nxt <CR>ws<C-R>n<Esc>/^row <CR>wcw3<Esc>/^col <CR>wcw8<Esc>/^rot <CR>wr0/^tick <CR>wcw0<Esc>/^then <CR>wcwframe<Esc>/^else <CR>wcwover<Esc>/^:fit <CR>f l"ay$@a
:over /^:q1 <CR>f l"qy$/^:frameo <CR>f l"ay$@a
:q0 gg
:q1 ZQ
" Park-Miller: seed * 16807 mod (2^31 - 1), as five times 7; the piece is seed mod 7.
:draw /^:t7 <CR>f l"ay$@a/^:t7 <CR>f l"ay$@a/^:t7 <CR>f l"ay$@a/^:t7 <CR>f l"ay$@a/^:t7 <CR>f l"ay$@a/^seed <CR>w"nyiw/^dig <CR>wi<C-R>n<Esc>/^rem <CR>wr0/^:dloop <CR>f l"ay$@a/^rem <CR>w"nyl/^P<C-R>n:<CR>f:l"nyl/^drawn <CR>ws<C-R>n<Esc>
" seed * 7: long multiplication into "prod", then mod 2^31 - 1 in m7.
:t7 /^seed <CR>w"nyiw/^mul <CR>wi<C-R>n<Esc>/^prod <CR>wC|@s<Esc>/^carry <CR>wr0/^:mloop <CR>f l"ay$@a/^then <CR>wcwmcarry<Esc>/^else <CR>wcwnop<Esc>gg/^carry [1-9]\|^ELSE|<CR>ml$h"ay$@a/^prod <CR>w"nyiw/^w <CR>wcw<C-R>n<Esc>/^:m7 <CR>f l"ay$@a
:mloop /^then <CR>wcwmstep<Esc>/^else <CR>wcwnop<Esc>gg/^mul \d\|^ELSE|<CR>ml$h"ay$@a
:mstep 'lf|h"nylx/^carry <CR>w"myl/^x<C-R>m<C-R>n:<CR>f:l"nyll"myl/^prod <CR>wi<C-R>n<Esc>/^carry <CR>ws<C-R>m<Esc>/^:mloop <CR>f l"ay$@a
:mcarry /^carry <CR>w"nyl/^prod <CR>wi<C-R>n<Esc>
:m7 /^w <CR>w999999999<C-X>999999999<C-X>147483649<C-X>/^then <CR>wcwm7end<Esc>/^else <CR>wcwm7<Esc>gg/^w -\|^ELSE|<CR>ml$h"ay$@a
:m7end /^w <CR>w999999999<C-A>999999999<C-A>147483649<C-A>/^w <CR>w"nyiw/^seed <CR>wcw<C-R>n<Esc>
" seed mod 7, one decimal digit at a time from the left, from the "m" table.
:dloop /^then <CR>wcwdstep<Esc>/^else <CR>wcwnop<Esc>gg/^dig \d\|^ELSE|<CR>ml$h"ay$@a
:dstep 'lw"nylx/^rem <CR>w"myl/^m<C-R>m<C-R>n:<CR>f:l"nyl/^rem <CR>ws<C-R>n<Esc>/^:dloop <CR>f l"ay$@a
" The frame: the board, the piece, the decoration.
:frame /^:fbase <CR>f l"ay$@a/^:stampf <CR>f l"ay$@a/^:fdecor <CR>f l"ay$@a
:frameo /^:fbase <CR>f l"ay$@a/^F$<CR>12j5|10r!/^:fdecor <CR>f l"ay$@a/^:banner <CR>f l"ay$@a
" Copy the 20 board lines between F and E, with two lines above them for the title.
:fbase 3G"r20yy/^E$<CR>"rP/^F$<CR>o<Esc>/^F$<CR>mg/^E$<CR>me
:stampf /^row <CR>w"ryiw/^col <CR>w"cyiw/^cmd <CR>wC'g<C-R>rj<C-R>c|<Esc>04l"by$/^cur <CR>w"pyl/^rot <CR>w"oyl/^S<C-R>p<C-R>o:<CR>f:l"xy$@b@x
" Walls off, borders and side panel on (block inserts and a block paste), paint, title.
:fdecor 'g3j0<C-V>19j3ld'g3j11|<C-V>19j$d'g3j0<C-V>19jI <C-V><Esc>[38;5;60m║<C-V><Esc>[m<Esc>'g3j$<C-V>19j$A<C-V><Esc>[38;5;60m║<C-V><Esc>[m<Esc>/^:panel <CR>f l"ay$@a'g3j$<C-V>19j$A<C-V><Esc>[K<Esc>'g22jo <C-V><Esc>[38;5;60m╚════════════════════╝<C-V><Esc>[m<C-V><Esc>[K<Esc>/^:paint <CR>f l"ky$@k'gjS<C-V><Esc>[H  <C-V><Esc>[1;38;5;75mV I M T R I S<C-V><Esc>[m<C-V><Esc>[K<Esc>'g2jS <C-V><Esc>[38;5;60m╔════════════════════╗<C-V><Esc>[m<C-V><Esc>[K<Esc>
:banner /\%>'g!\{10}<CR>10s<C-V><Esc>[1;7m     GAME  OVER     <C-V><Esc>[m<Esc>
" Copy the side panel below E, fill in the numbers and the preview, yank it as a block.
:panel /^PANEL{<CR>j"t20yy/^E$<CR>"tp/^E$<CR>mw/^score <CR>w"nyiw/\%>'w@S<CR>2s<C-R>n<Esc>/^level <CR>w"nyiw/\%>'w@V<CR>2s<C-R>n<Esc>/^lines <CR>w"nyiw/\%>'w@L<CR>2s<C-R>n<Esc>/^nxt <CR>w"pyl/^N<C-R>p:<CR>f:l"uyt|f|l"vy$/\%>'w@0<CR>2s<C-R>u<Esc>/\%>'w@1<CR>2s<C-R>v<Esc>'wj0<C-V>19j$"py'wj20"_dd'g3j$"pp
" Paint the next cell from the C table, until the search falls through to PAINTED.
:paint 'g/\%<'e[.IOTSZJL]\|^PAINTED|<CR>mx"nyl?\V\^C<C-R>n:<CR>f:l"ay$@a
:evx gg
" ---- tables: F fit regex and S stamp per piece and rotation, N preview rows,
" P piece for a remainder, m remainder of 10r + d by 7, x 7d + c as digit and carry,
" C the colour of a cell, PANEL the side panel, F to E the frame, then the fallbacks.
FI0:\_.\{22}\.\.\.\.
